{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a count of Tripoli who ruled from 1155 to 1183. He was a prominent figure in the Crusades and a key leader in the defense of the county against Muslim incursions. His reign saw significant territorial expansion and consolidation of Tripoli's power.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension*\n\nRaymond III was born in 1126 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and his wife Gertrude. He inherited the county upon the death of his father in 1155. His early reign was marked by internal conflicts and challenges from neighboring Muslim rulers. He skillfully navigated these complexities establishing alliances and maintaining a relatively stable government. He proved a capable military leader quickly solidifying his authority. He was known for his piety and his efforts to foster religious unity.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Conflicts*\n\nRaymond III's reign was dominated by military campaigns against Muslim forces. He engaged in numerous battles securing Tripoli's borders and expanding its territory. He fought against the Almohad dynasty and the Zangian dynasty both of whom posed significant threats to the county's independence. His military successes earned him the respect of his vassals and the admiration of his people. He implemented effective defensive strategies and built fortifications to protect Tripoli from attack. He also promoted the development of a professional army.\n\n*Legacy and Decline*\n\nRaymond III's reign is considered a golden age for the County of Tripoli. He oversaw a period of economic prosperity and cultural flourishing. He fostered trade and attracted merchants from across Europe. His leadership helped to maintain Tripoli's position as a major power in the Levant. However his reign eventually ended with his death in 1183. After his death the county faced internal strife and external pressures leading to a gradual decline in its power and influence. He is remembered as a courageous and effective ruler who defended Tripoli against overwhelming odds. His legacy continues to be studied by historians who view him as a pivotal figure in the history of the Crusades and the Levant. He is regarded as a strong and effective ruler who successfully defended his county against numerous enemies.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.14342188835144043}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -4.5060096454108134e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.0798519179224968}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.04111293703317642}, {"token": "▁count", "logprob": -2.6321768760681152}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -0.076082743704319}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": -0.011413871310651302}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.2440190315246582}, {"token": "▁ruled", "logprob": -0.2878400683403015}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -0.004115920979529619}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.003056142944842577}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00019226610311307013}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0019722788129001856}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -2.060868978500366}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -0.05743550509214401}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.0843970775604248}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0006597249885089695}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -8.49926145747304e-05}, {"token": "8", "logprob": -0.06938929855823517}, {"token": "3", "logprob": -0.911524772644043}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.019212933257222176}, {"token": "▁He", "logprob": -0.0036030393093824387}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.18094885349273682}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.10580378025770187}, {"token": "▁prominent", "logprob": -0.31300434470176697}, {"token": "▁figure", "logprob": -0.0026058547664433718}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.02706337906420231}, {"token": "▁the", "lo